{"id":"mahabharata-9-049","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":49,"title":"एकोनपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 49 · Asita Devala and the Siddhas","summary":{"en":"Asita Devala, the sage who lived there as a householder, is visited by the sage Jaigishavya and the two live together in ascetic rivalry. Devala is amazed by Jaigishavya's yoga and asks the Siddhas about him, then Balarama bathes and goes on.","kn":"ಅಲ್ಲಿ ಗೃಹಸ್ಥನಾಗಿ ವಾಸಿಸುತ್ತಿದ್ದ ಅಸಿತ ದೇವಲ ಋಷಿಯನ್ನು ಜೈಗೀಷವ್ಯ ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗಿ ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ತಪೋ ಸ್ಪರ್ಧೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ವಾಸಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಜೈಗೀಷವ್ಯನ ಯೋಗಕ್ಕೆ ಬೆರಗಾದ ದೇವಲ ಸಿದ್ಧರನ್ನು ಅವನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಬಲರಾಮ ಸ್ನಾನ ಮಾಡಿ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वहाँ गृहस्थ के रूप में रहने वाले ऋषि असित देवल से जैगीषव्य मिलते हैं और दोनों तप-स्पर्धा में साथ रहते हैं। जैगीषव्य के योग से चकित देवल सिद्धों से उनके बारे में पूछते हैं, फिर बलराम स्नान कर आगे बढ़ते हैं।","te":"అక్కడ గృహస్థుగా ఉన్న అసిత దేవల ఋషిని జైగీషవ్యుడు కలవగా ఇద్దరూ తపస్సు పోటీలో కలిసి ఉంటారు. జైగీషవ్యుని యోగానికి ఆశ్చర్యపడిన దేవలుడు సిద్ధులను అతని గురించి అడుగుతాడు; బలరాముడు స్నానం చేసి ముందుకు సాగుతాడు.","ta":"அங்கு இல்லறத்தானாக வாழ்ந்த முனிவர் அசித தேவலரைச் சைகீஷவ்யர் சந்திக்க, இருவரும் தவப் போட்டியில் ஒன்றாக வாழ்கின்றனர். சைகீஷவ்யரின் யோகத்தால் வியந்த தேவலர் சித்தர்களிடம் அவரைப் பற்றிக் கேட்கிறார்; பலராமன் நீராடிச் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"അവിടെ ഗൃഹസ്ഥനായി ജീവിച്ച അസിത ദേവലനെ ജൈഗീഷവ്യൻ എന്ന ഋഷി സന്ദർശിക്കുന്നു; ഇരുവരും തപോമത്സരത്തിൽ ഒന്നിച്ചു ജീവിക്കുന്നു. ജൈഗീഷവ്യന്റെ യോഗശക്തിയിൽ അത്ഭുതപ്പെട്ട ദേവലൻ സിദ്ധന്മാരോട് അദ്ദേഹത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ചോദിക്കുന്നു; പിന്നെ ബലരാമൻ സ്നാനം ചെയ്ത് യാത്ര തുടരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.49; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"सारस्वतपर्व","titleEn":"Sarasvata Parva (Balarama's pilgrimage on the Sarasvati)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मिन्नेव तु धर्मात्मा वसति स्म तपोधनः ।\nगार्हस्थ्यं धर्ममास्थाय असितो देवलः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that same place, long ago, there lived the righteous Asita Devala, rich in austerity, who followed the householder's way of life."}},{"n":2,"text":"धर्मनित्यः शुचिर्दान्तो न्यस्तदण्डो महातपाः ।\nकर्मणा मनसा वाचा समः सर्वेषु जन्तुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devoted always to dharma, pure and self-controlled, he had laid down all violence; that great ascetic treated every living creature alike in deed, thought and word."}},{"n":3,"text":"अक्रोधनो महाराज तुल्यनिन्दाप्रियाप्रियः ।\nकाञ्चने लोष्टके चैव समदर्शी महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, he was free of anger, held blame and praise, the pleasant and the unpleasant, as equal, and looked on gold and a clod of earth with the same eye."}},{"n":4,"text":"देवताः पूजयन्नित्यमतिथींश्च द्विजैः सह ।\nब्रह्मचर्यरतो नित्यं सदा धर्मपरायणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He constantly honoured the gods and guests together with the brahmins, was always devoted to celibate discipline, and was ever intent on dharma."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततोऽभ्येत्य महाराज योगमास्थाय भिक्षुकः ।\nजैगीषव्यो मुनिर्धीमांस्तस्मिंस्तीर्थे समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O great king, the wise sage Jaigishavya came there as a wandering mendicant, devoted to yoga, and settled in concentration at that sacred ford."}},{"n":6,"text":"देवलस्याश्रमे राजन्न्यवसत्स महाद्युतिः ।\nयोगनित्यो महाराज सिद्धिं प्राप्तो महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, that radiant sage stayed in Devala's hermitage, always absorbed in yoga, a great ascetic who had attained perfection."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं तत्र वसमानं तु जैगीषव्यं महामुनिम् ।\nदेवलो दर्शयन्नेव नैवायुञ्जत धर्मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though Jaigishavya was living there before his eyes, Devala, keeping to dharma, did not engage him in conversation."}},{"n":8,"text":"एवं तयोर्महाराज दीर्घकालो व्यतिक्रमत् ।\nजैगीषव्यं मुनिं चैव न ददर्शाथ देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, great king, a long time passed for the two of them, and Devala would not see the sage Jaigishavya at other times."}},{"n":9,"text":"आहारकाले मतिमान्परिव्राड्जनमेजय ।\nउपातिष्ठत धर्मज्ञो भैक्षकाले स देवलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O Janamejaya, at mealtime the wise wandering monk, knower of dharma, would come to Devala at the hour for alms."}},{"n":10,"text":"स दृष्ट्वा भिक्षुरूपेण प्राप्तं तत्र महामुनिम् ।\nगौरवं परमं चक्रे प्रीतिं च विपुलां तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the great sage arrive in the form of a beggar, Devala showed him the highest respect and great affection."}},{"n":11,"text":"देवलस्तु यथाशक्ति पूजयामास भारत ।\nऋषिदृष्टेन विधिना समा बह्व्यः समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O Bharata, for many years Devala, with a collected mind, honoured him as best he could, by the method taught by the seers."}},{"n":12,"text":"कदाचित्तस्य नृपते देवलस्य महात्मनः ।\nचिन्ता सुमहती जाता मुनिं दृष्ट्वा महाद्युतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, O king, a great worry arose in the mind of the noble Devala as he looked at that radiant sage."}},{"n":13,"text":"समास्तु समतिक्रान्ता बह्व्यः पूजयतो मम ।\nन चायमलसो भिक्षुरभ्यभाषत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"He thought: \"Many years have gone by while I have been honouring him, and yet this idle mendicant has never said a word to me.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"एवं विगणयन्नेव स जगाम महोदधिम् ।\nअन्तरिक्षचरः श्रीमान्कलशं गृह्य देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reflecting in this way, the splendid Devala took his water-pot and went, travelling through the sky, to the great ocean."}},{"n":15,"text":"गच्छन्नेव स धर्मात्मा समुद्रं सरितां पतिम् ।\nजैगीषव्यं ततोऽपश्यद्गतं प्रागेव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the righteous one was going to the ocean, the lord of rivers, O Bharata, he saw Jaigishavya, who had reached it before him."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः सविस्मयश्चिन्तां जगामाथासितः प्रभुः ।\nकथं भिक्षुरयं प्राप्तः समुद्रे स्नात एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the powerful Asita was filled with wonder and thought: how has this beggar come here and already bathed in the ocean?"}},{"n":17,"text":"इत्येवं चिन्तयामास महर्षिरसितस्तदा ।\nस्नात्वा समुद्रे विधिवच्छुचिर्जप्यं जजाप ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the great seer Asita pondered; then he bathed in the ocean as the rule requires and, being pure, recited his prayers."}},{"n":18,"text":"कृतजप्याह्निकः श्रीमानाश्रमं च जगाम ह ।\nकलशं जलपूर्णं वै गृहीत्वा जनमेजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having finished his prayers and daily rites, the glorious one took his pot filled with water and went back to his hermitage, O Janamejaya."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः स प्रविशन्नेव स्वमाश्रमपदं मुनिः ।\nआसीनमाश्रमे तत्र जैगीषव्यमपश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sage entered his own hermitage, he saw Jaigishavya sitting there."}},{"n":20,"text":"न व्याहरति चैवैनं जैगीषव्यः कथंचन ।\nकाष्ठभूतोऽऽश्रमपदे वसति स्म महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jaigishavya did not speak to him at all; that great ascetic stayed in the hermitage as still as a block of wood."}},{"n":21,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा चाप्लुतं तोये सागरे सागरोपमम् ।\nप्रविष्टमाश्रमं चापि पूर्वमेव ददर्श सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had seen him bathing in the ocean, vast as the sea itself, and now saw that he had entered the hermitage before him."}},{"n":22,"text":"असितो देवलो राजंश्चिन्तयामास बुद्धिमान् ।\nदृष्टः प्रभावं तपसो जैगीषव्यस्य योगजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, the wise Asita Devala, having seen the power that Jaigishavya's yoga had given his austerity, began to think."}},{"n":23,"text":"चिन्तयामास राजेन्द्र तदा स मुनिसत्तमः ।\nमया दृष्टः समुद्रे च आश्रमे च कथं त्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O best of kings, that foremost sage thought: \"How is it that I saw him at the ocean and now again in the hermitage?\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं विगणयन्नेव स मुनिर्मन्त्रपारगः ।\nउत्पपाताश्रमात्तस्मादन्तरिक्षं विशां पते ।\nजिज्ञासार्थं तदा भिक्षोर्जैगीषव्यस्य देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pondering thus, the sage, a master of mantras, rose from the hermitage into the sky, O lord of men, wishing to test the mendicant Jaigishavya."}},{"n":25,"text":"सोऽन्तरिक्षचरान्सिद्धान्समपश्यत्समाहितान् ।\nजैगीषव्यं च तैः सिद्धैः पूज्यमानमपश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he saw the Siddhas who move through the sky, gathered in concentration, and he saw Jaigishavya being honoured by those Siddhas."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततोऽसितः सुसंरब्धो व्यवसायी दृढव्रतः ।\nअपश्यद्वै दिवं यान्तं जैगीषव्यं स देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Asita, intent, resolute and firm in his vows, saw Jaigishavya going up to heaven."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्माच्च पितृलोकं तं व्रजन्तं सोऽन्वपश्यत ।\nपितृलोकाच्च तं यान्तं याम्यं लोकमपश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"From there Devala saw him going on to the world of the ancestors, and from the world of the ancestors to the realm of Yama."}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्मादपि समुत्पत्य सोमलोकमभिष्टुतम् ।\nव्रजन्तमन्वपश्यत्स जैगीषव्यं महामुनिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rising from there too, he followed the great sage Jaigishavya as he went to the praised world of Soma."}},{"n":29,"text":"लोकान्समुत्पतन्तं च शुभानेकान्तयाजिनाम् ।\nततोऽग्निहोत्रिणां लोकांस्तेभ्यश्चाप्युत्पपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jaigishavya rose beyond the fair worlds of those who sacrifice with single-minded devotion, and then beyond the worlds of those who keep the agnihotra."}},{"n":30,"text":"दर्शं च पौर्णमासं च ये यजन्ति तपोधनाः ।\nतेभ्यः स ददृशे धीमाँल्लोकेभ्यः पशुयाजिनाम् ।\nव्रजन्तं लोकममलमपश्यद्देवपूजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devala, the wise, saw him pass the worlds of those ascetics who perform the new-moon and full-moon sacrifices and of those who offer animal sacrifices, and go on to a spotless world honoured by the gods."}},{"n":31,"text":"चातुर्मास्यैर्बहुविधैर्यजन्ते ये तपोधनाः ।\nतेषां स्थानं तथा यान्तं तथाग्निष्टोमयाजिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw him reach the abode of ascetics who worship with the various Chaturmasya sacrifices, and of those who perform the Agnishtoma."}},{"n":32,"text":"अग्निष्टुतेन च तथा ये यजन्ति तपोधनाः ।\nतत्स्थानमनुसंप्राप्तमन्वपश्यत देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devala saw him arrive at the place of those who sacrifice with the Agnishtuta rite."}},{"n":33,"text":"वाजपेयं क्रतुवरं तथा बहुसुवर्णकम् ।\nआहरन्ति महाप्राज्ञास्तेषां लोकेष्वपश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw him among the worlds of the greatly wise who perform the Vajapeya, the best of sacrifices, with its abundant gold."}},{"n":34,"text":"यजन्ते पुण्डरीकेण राजसूयेन चैव ये ।\nतेषां लोकेष्वपश्यच्च जैगीषव्यं स देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devala saw Jaigishavya in the worlds of those who sacrifice with the Pundarika and the Rajasuya."}},{"n":35,"text":"अश्वमेधं क्रतुवरं नरमेधं तथैव च ।\nआहरन्ति नरश्रेष्ठास्तेषां लोकेष्वपश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw him in the worlds of those best of men who perform the Ashvamedha, the finest of sacrifices, and the Naramedha."}},{"n":36,"text":"सर्वमेधं च दुष्प्रापं तथा सौत्रामणिं च ये ।\nतेषां लोकेष्वपश्यच्च जैगीषव्यं स देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devala saw Jaigishavya in the worlds of those who perform the hard-to-obtain Sarvamedha and the Sautramani."}},{"n":37,"text":"द्वादशाहैश्च सत्रैर्ये यजन्ते विविधैर्नृप ।\nतेषां लोकेष्वपश्यच्च जैगीषव्यं स देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, Devala saw Jaigishavya in the worlds of those who sacrifice with the many kinds of twelve-day sacrificial sessions."}},{"n":38,"text":"मित्रावरुणयोर्लोकानादित्यानां तथैव च ।\nसलोकतामनुप्राप्तमपश्यत ततोऽसितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Asita saw him attain equality of world with Mitra and Varuna and with the Adityas."}},{"n":39,"text":"रुद्राणां च वसूनां च स्थानं यच्च बृहस्पतेः ।\nतानि सर्वाण्यतीतं च समपश्यत्ततोऽसितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Asita saw him pass beyond them all: the abode of the Rudras and the Vasus, and the place of Brihaspati."}},{"n":40,"text":"आरुह्य च गवां लोकं प्रयान्तं ब्रह्मसत्रिणाम् ।\nलोकानपश्यद्गच्छन्तं जैगीषव्यं ततोऽसितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Climbing up to the world of the cows, where those who perform Brahma sessions go, Asita saw Jaigishavya moving on through those worlds."}},{"n":41,"text":"त्रीँल्लोकानपरान्विप्रमुत्पतन्तं स्वतेजसा ।\nपतिव्रतानां लोकांश्च व्रजन्तं सोऽन्वपश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw the brahmin, by his own radiance, rise beyond three further worlds, and go to the worlds of devoted and faithful wives."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततो मुनिवरं भूयो जैगीषव्यमथासितः ।\nनान्वपश्यत योगस्थमन्तर्हितमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O subduer of foes, Asita no longer saw the best of sages, Jaigishavya, who had vanished, steadfast in yoga."}},{"n":43,"text":"सोऽचिन्तयन्महाभागो जैगीषव्यस्य देवलः ।\nप्रभावं सुव्रतत्वं च सिद्धिं योगस्य चातुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The greatly fortunate Devala reflected on Jaigishavya's power, his firm vows and the matchless perfection of his yoga."}},{"n":44,"text":"असितोऽपृच्छत तदा सिद्धाँल्लोकेषु सत्तमान् ।\nप्रयतः प्राञ्जलिर्भूत्वा धीरस्तान्ब्रह्मसत्रिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Asita, self-controlled and steady, with joined palms asked the best of the Siddhas, those performers of Brahma sessions, in those worlds."}},{"n":45,"text":"जैगीषव्यं न पश्यामि तं शंसत महौजसम् ।\nएतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं परं कौतूहलं हि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said: \"I do not see Jaigishavya. Tell me where that mighty one is; I want to hear this, for my curiosity is very great.\""}},{"text":"सिद्धा ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The Siddhas said:"}},{"n":46,"text":"शृणु देवल भूतार्थं शंसतां नो दृढव्रत ।\nजैगीषव्यो गतो लोकं शाश्वतं ब्रह्मणोऽव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, Devala, firm in your vows, to the truth as we tell it: Jaigishavya has gone to the eternal, imperishable world of Brahma."}},{"n":47,"text":"स श्रुत्वा वचनं तेषां सिद्धानां ब्रह्मसत्रिणाम् ।\nअसितो देवलस्तूर्णमुत्पपात पपात च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words of the Siddhas, those performers of Brahma sessions, Asita Devala at once leapt upward, and then fell down."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततः सिद्धास्त ऊचुर्हि देवलं पुनरेव ह ।\nन देवल गतिस्तत्र तव गन्तुं तपोधन ।\nब्रह्मणः सदनं विप्र जैगीषव्यो यदाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Siddhas said to Devala once more: \"Devala, rich in austerity, you cannot go there, to the abode of Brahma, brahmin, which Jaigishavya has reached.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"तेषां तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा सिद्धानां देवलः पुनः ।\nआनुपूर्व्येण लोकांस्तान्सर्वानवततार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those words of the Siddhas, Devala came back down through all those worlds in due order."}},{"n":50,"text":"स्वमाश्रमपदं पुण्यमाजगाम पतंगवत् ।\nप्रविशन्नेव चापश्यज्जैगीषव्यं स देवलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He returned to his own sacred hermitage as swiftly as a bird and, as he entered, saw Jaigishavya there."}},{"n":51,"text":"ततो बुद्ध्या व्यगणयद्देवलो धर्मयुक्तया ।\nदृष्ट्वा प्रभावं तपसो जैगीषव्यस्य योगजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Devala, seeing the power that Jaigishavya's yoga had given his austerity, reasoned with his mind, now set on dharma."}},{"n":52,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीन्महात्मानं जैगीषव्यं स देवलः ।\nविनयावनतो राजन्नुपसर्प्य महामुनिम् ।\nमोक्षधर्मं समास्थातुमिच्छेयं भगवन्नहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, humbly bowing, Devala approached the great sage Jaigishavya and said to that noble one: \"Revered sir, I wish to take up the dharma of liberation.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा उपदेशं चकार सः ।\nविधिं च योगस्य परं कार्याकार्यं च शास्त्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, Jaigishavya instructed him, teaching the supreme method of yoga and, from the scriptures, what is to be done and not done."}},{"n":54,"text":"संन्यासकृतबुद्धिं तं ततो दृष्ट्वा महातपाः ।\nसर्वाश्चास्य क्रियाश्चक्रे विधिदृष्टेन कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that Devala had resolved on renunciation, the great ascetic performed all of his rites according to the prescribed method."}},{"n":55,"text":"संन्यासकृतबुद्धिं तं भूतानि पितृभिः सह ।\nततो दृष्ट्वा प्ररुरुदुः कोऽस्मान्संविभजिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him resolved on renunciation, the beings together with the ancestors wept, saying: \"Who will now provide for us?\""}},{"n":56,"text":"देवलस्तु वचः श्रुत्वा भूतानां करुणं तथा ।\nदिशो दश व्याहरतां मोक्षं त्यक्तुं मनो दधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that piteous cry of the beings, Devala resolved to give up liberation, as they called out from the ten directions."}},{"n":57,"text":"ततस्तु फलमूलानि पवित्राणि च भारत ।\nपुष्पाण्योषधयश्चैव रोरूयन्ते सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O Bharata, the fruits and roots, the sacred herbs, the flowers and the plants cried out in their thousands."}},{"n":58,"text":"पुनर्नो देवलः क्षुद्रो नूनं छेत्स्यति दुर्मतिः ।\nअभयं सर्वभूतेभ्यो यो दत्त्वा नावबुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said: \"This petty, ill-minded Devala will surely cut us down again, he who gave safety to all beings and does not understand it.\""}},{"n":59,"text":"ततो भूयो व्यगणयत्स्वबुद्ध्या मुनिसत्तमः ।\nमोक्षे गार्हस्थ्यधर्मे वा किं नु श्रेयस्करं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the best of sages weighed the matter again by his own judgement: which is better, liberation or the householder's dharma?"}},{"n":60,"text":"इति निश्चित्य मनसा देवलो राजसत्तम ।\nत्यक्त्वा गार्हस्थ्यधर्मं स मोक्षधर्ममरोचयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having decided this in his mind, O best of kings, Devala gave up the householder's dharma and chose the dharma of liberation."}},{"n":61,"text":"एवमादीनि संचिन्त्य देवलो निश्चयात्ततः ।\nप्राप्तवान्परमां सिद्धिं परं योगं च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reflecting on such things, Devala, firm in his resolve, attained supreme perfection and the highest yoga, O Bharata."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततो देवाः समागम्य बृहस्पतिपुरोगमाः ।\nजैगीषव्यं तपश्चास्य प्रशंसन्ति तपस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the gods, led by Brihaspati, gathered and the ascetics praised Jaigishavya and his austerity."}},{"n":63,"text":"अथाब्रवीदृषिवरो देवान्वै नारदस्तदा ।\nजैगीषव्ये तपो नास्ति विस्मापयति योऽसितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great seer Narada said to the gods: \"There is no austerity in Jaigishavya, who has made Asita marvel.\""}},{"n":64,"text":"तमेवंवादिनं धीरं प्रत्यूचुस्ते दिवौकसः ।\nमैवमित्येव शंसन्तो जैगीषव्यं महामुनिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those dwellers in heaven answered the steadfast Narada as he spoke: \"Do not say so,\" praising the great sage Jaigishavya."}},{"n":65,"text":"तत्राप्युपस्पृश्य ततो महात्मा\nदत्त्वा च वित्तं हलभृद्द्विजेभ्यः ।\nअवाप्य धर्मं परमार्यकर्मा\nजगाम सोमस्य महत्स तीर्थम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too, the great-souled one bathed, gave wealth to the brahmins, the plough-bearer Balarama of noble deeds, and having gained dharma went to the great sacred ford of Soma."}}]}]}